        <referenceFunction amount="1.0" category="material, obsolete" datasetRelatesToProduct="true" generalComment="The dataset can be applied to describe an average room door. The door frame is made of massive wood, the door leaf is made of wood with a glass insert (62 % wood, 38% glass). The lock, door handles and frame joints are fabricated from steel. Data are based on a door of 0.8x2.0 m and scaled to 1m2. 1 m2 of the wooden inner door weighs 27.6 kg. The functional life time for the door frame is 50 years, for the door leaf it is 30 years. \nGeography: Data from producers in Switzerland.\nTechnology: The technology represents average European production.\nVersion: 2.2\nEnergy values: Undefined\nLocal category: Bauteile\nLocal subcategory: Türen\nUVEK 2022 source file:07154.XML\n\n&#10;UUID: 803af2c7-5f58-377f-95fc-e461084c9ff9" includedProcesses="This dataset describes the production of 1m2 (visible area) inner door, including the processes for the installation. Not included are transports from plant to construction site." infrastructureProcess="false" localCategory="material, obsolete" localName="xxx Door, inner, glass-wood, at plant" localSubCategory="construction, obsolete\doors, obsolete" name="xxx Door, inner, glass-wood, at plant" subCategory="construction, obsolete\doors, obsolete" unit="m2"/>
